{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>With their flames</b>. Our Rabbis said (Sanhedrin 67b) that these are acts of sorcery and are performed by means of angels of destruction. The word is derived from \"flaming fire\" (אֵשׁ לוֹהֵט) (Psalms 104:4), \"a flame burns the wicked\" (לֶהָבָה תְּלַהֵט רְשָׁעִים) (ibid. 106:18). The meaning is that they are performed by means of flames — angels of fire — inflaming a person without his knowledge, burning within him without his taking notice, as in the matter of \"and YHWH opened the eyes of the young man of Elisha, and behold, chariots of fire and horses of fire\" (II Kings 6:17). And perhaps the angels dwelling in the air, in the spheres of the elements — whom they call officers — are so called as well. I will explain further with the help of the Rock (Leviticus 16:8; ibid. 17:7; Deuteronomy 18:10, 14). But concerning \"בְּלָטֵיהֶם\" (Exodus 8:3), they said (Sanhedrin 67b) that these are demons, and the word is derived from \"לָט\" — \"they spoke to David secretly (בַלָּט)\" (I Samuel 18:22) — for demons come secretly, since they possess bodies of imperceptible air. This is why it says \"to the wise men and to the sorcerers,\" for the masters of incantations and those who gather demons were their chiefs and elders, while \"the charmers of Egypt\" includes both groups, though we do not know the derivation of the word. Rabbi Abraham said (Ibn Ezra on Exodus 7:11) that it is an Egyptian expression or a Chaldean one, for we find it only in the words of both of them. But the closer view, according to Rashi's words (Genesis 41:8), is that it is a compound Aramaic word — חַר טָמֵי — those who bore into bones, for it is well known that most of the craft involves bones of the dead or bones of living animals, as they mentioned in connection with the יִדְּעוֹנִי (Sanhedrin 65b)."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:16:22.287881252Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}